<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Lebanese Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1926 CE – present · capital Beirut</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The republic of Lebanon, founded under French mandate in 1926, whose sharing of power among religious communities defines its politics.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 23 May 1926 the constitution adopted by the representative council turned <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/greater-lebanon">Greater Lebanon</a> into the Lebanese Republic, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-debbas">Charles Debbas</a> as first president, still under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-mandate-for-syria-and-the-lebanon">French Mandate for Syria and the Lebanon</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The unwritten <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-pact">National Pact</a> of 1943, agreed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bechara-el-khoury">Bechara El Khoury</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riad-al-solh">Riad Al Solh</a>, reserved the presidency for a Maronite, the premiership for a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> and the speakership for a Shia. Independence was won in November 1943. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/beirut">Beirut</a> became a banking, trade and cultural centre, but sectarian and social tensions, the 1958 crisis and the presence of Palestinian armed groups led to the civil war of 1975-1990.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taif-agreement">Taif Agreement</a> of 1989 ended the war, though Syrian troops stayed until 2005, leaving after the assassination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rafic-hariri">Rafic Hariri</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a> then suffered the 2006 war, the 2019 financial collapse, the 2020 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/beirut">Beirut</a> port explosion and the 2024 war between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-israel">Israel</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hezbollah">Hezbollah</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-aoun">Joseph Aoun</a> became president in 2025.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lebanese-republic.jpg" alt="Lebanese Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Henri Pharaon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Lebanon.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1926 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Beirut</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bechara El Khoury, Fouad Chehab, Rafic Hariri</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity, Sunni and Shia Islam, Druze</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/lebanon">Lebanon</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lebanon, Republic of Lebanon</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1976&amp;focus=lebanese-republic" aria-label="Lebanese Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5585 949 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lebanese Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5905 1205L5905 1205M5905 1205L5905 1205"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5905 1205h0M5905 1205h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5905 1205h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5905 1205h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Beirut. <a href="/atlas?year=1976&amp;focus=lebanese-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
